{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And from the sanctuary he shall not go out.</b> He does not follow the bier (Sanhedrin 18). And furthermore, our Rabbis learned from here that a High Priest offers the sacrifice while an onen — and so the verse implies: even if his father and mother died, he need not leave the sanctuary but performs the Divine service." "<b>And he shall not profane the sanctuary.</b> For he does not thereby profane the Divine service, since Scripture permitted it to him — whereas a common priest who served while an onen has profaned it (Zevachim 16; Sanhedrin 8)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:33.950586430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}